      "problem": "$-49\\text{ mod }7=$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n-49≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-49$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-49≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n-49=(-7)\\cdot 7+0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is $0.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49 & ≡-49+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-49+7\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-49+49 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is $0.$",
